  "scope": "Prior-predictive numerical control; fuel envelope conditioned; no accident calibration; coordinate intervals are not joint geographic areas",
  "method_reference": {
    "url": "https://sites.stat.columbia.edu/gelman/research/unpublished/sbc.pdf",
    "locator": "pp. 3\u20135: prior-predictive repetition, empirical CDF limitations and computational scope"
  },
  "limitations": [
    "Only 4 generated data sets in this comparison; binomial uncertainty is substantial.",
    "Weighted interacting particle rows are not independent posterior draws; these CDF diagnostics are not an exact independent-rank SBC test.",
    "Generator shares flight and SATCOM equations with inference. Independent physical and equation checks remain necessary.",
    "Generating routes were accepted by an independent uniform draw against the same remaining-fuel-envelope probability used in inference. Acceptance uses no SATCOM measurement or noise value. This checks computation conditional on that envelope, not the physical validity of the fuel model or an exact exhaustion trajectory.",
    "The accident-specific initial proposal is disabled for this control. A single proposal-component choice covers all commands until the next physical contact. The complete mixture density is compensated once; event-time corrections stay separate. The command factor is bounded by5 perinterval, not percommand; this does not bound posterior concentration."
  ],
